Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Riemannian Infrageometry", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Abstract written by Pavel Hajek on 18 October 2026.", \
"TI"]], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Riemannian Infrageometry describes and distinguishes graphs as ",
 StyleBox["geometric substrates",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". In contrast, synthetic infrageometry asks only whether certain postulates \
are satisfied by the substrate so that its propositions about geometric \
objects hold."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Riemann viewed space as an infinitesimal webbing of paths and, by imposing \
conditions on the infinitesimal length element, arrived at the ",
 StyleBox["quadratic metric tensor",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " as the lowest-order data satisfying those conditions. This split \
continuous geometry into a manifold, which carries the topology and global \
analysis, and a Riemannian structure. This led people such as Gromov to ask \
about the moduli space of Riemannian structures on a fixed manifold, or, \
conversely, to derive topological quantities from Riemannian ones."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In infrageometry, the discrete webbing of paths given by a graph is itself \
the geometric substrate, so no such split occurs. We relate infrageometry to \
continuous geometry through ",
 StyleBox["rescaled Gromov\[Dash]Hausdorff convergence",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", where the scaling is determined by the observer's scale. This yields a \
generalized definition of geometry: if a limit of rescaled graphs is a metric \
space arising from a Riemannian manifold, then that manifold is uniquely \
determined up to isomorphism."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A geodesic at observer scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7061f79a-7143-4912-bb9b-401efc6d24b2"],
 " of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6dd6f6c-3bca-4917-ad02-0232d173e824"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraGeodesic"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["germ", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9df620e-31f2-4c9b-b03c-8315edfb5974"],
 ", is a family of walks of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a871ecab-a519-4109-8e27-24ccbcc65dcd"],
 " that are shortest paths in every window of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96591348-4c24-4370-ab5c-c0ff74d7342a"],
 " edges. A representative can be found with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraGeodesic"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", "\[Ellipsis]", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04a29d91-2371-4db3-bd8e-74647657df25"],
 ", and the edge density of the corresponding multi-object with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["geodesic", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed780c3f-93d8-4100-8e4b-da0a581715ec"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can measure the volumes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraBall"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r0", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d60a0c4e-197e-430b-b806-26419b093a5f"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "0"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8b624c4c-ae5f-441c-9c86-0ad996efe93c"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraTube"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTube", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3efe571-5c45-4e10-81d4-8fd2bef442d8"],
 " for any ray or line through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af9d5508-9849-4cea-bd5b-e8ebdfa731b3"],
 " and any thickness ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba74081f-5860-4fe5-a837-c98147e519aa"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraCone"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCone", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14c8af44-e646-4c51-a7de-93ab35afb44c"],
 " for slope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8eb0d7a-ba33-4bb6-b6bb-506f7b3641ec"],
 ". Such measurements have asymptotic expansions in the continuous case and \
can be used to determine ",
 StyleBox["limiting curvature components",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". However, no sphere structure exists a priori on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraShell"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraShell", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ef1e3e2-b421-4c2a-a006-278275f41361"],
 ", so the limiting linear tensors can be compared only through histograms. \
We can also obtain the histogram of mutual distances between points, which \
constrains the limiting Riemannian manifold."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraTangentBundle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTangentBundle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88bd8be9-e920-467d-877f-cfdcb1a70668"],
 " which represents vectors at p by rays of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b39275b3-4574-4f1c-8f8a-8a7d155d0b6c"],
 ", and these are compactly encoded as chains in the spray graph at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045f0329-a119-4dba-8a08-a494f824b566"],
 ". We have an even simpler infra-bundle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraDisplacementBundle"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDisplacementBundle", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a84bf262-2f9a-492b-be9a-8a22ee7b7231"],
 ", that keeps only the endpoints of rays. We have a minimal model of the \
Levi-Civita connection, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/\
FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ab1a5b7-30e5-4149-a457-aa50d485790d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraParallelTransport"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraParallelTransport", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["walk", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4dd4138-47a7-45c0-af1e-18548261fa08"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We also have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMetricTensor"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMetricTensor", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8dfb3745-ad00-4b3b-bda2-d30990db7f88"],
 ", which computes shortest path projections of rays, displacement commutator \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["DisplacementCommutator"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementCommutator", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "314c9125-3c5c-44e0-ac9d-01250307051f"],
 ", and addition of displacements via midpoints with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["DisplacementSum"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementSum", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e8368e14-1c81-4b3b-a246-e29b0090a854"],
 ". These can be used to illustrate ",
 StyleBox["emergence of linearity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

